# =============================================================================
# Trivy suppressions
# =============================================================================
# Each entry below is a finding that Trivy is right to raise in general and
# that this project has consciously accepted. Nothing is suppressed because it
# was inconvenient; every line says what the risk is and why it stands.
#
# Review this file whenever the stack changes. A suppression that outlives its
# justification is worse than no scanning at all.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AVD-DS-0001 — image tag is ':latest'
#
# Three images float deliberately:
#   ollama/ollama          runtime and model formats move in lockstep; pinning
#                          an old runtime breaks new models
#   ghcr.io/open-webui     upstream publishes ':main' as its release channel
#   minio/minio, minio/mc  date-stamped release tags only, no stable minor tag
#
# Every other image in the lab is pinned. CI enforces that separately, by
# failing on any image with no tag at all.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AVD-DS-0001

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AVD-DS-0026 — no HEALTHCHECK instruction
#
# Healthchecks are defined in compose rather than baked into images the project
# does not build. CI verifies that every long-running service has one.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AVD-DS-0026

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AVD-DS-0002 — container runs as root
#
# Applies to the images this lab consumes but does not build. Where the
# upstream image supports it, the lab overrides the user explicitly: Traefik
# (1000), Prometheus (65534), Grafana (472), Loki (10001), Gitea (1000),
# Redis (redis), and nginx via the unprivileged variant.
#
# The remainder — Keycloak, Vault, PostgreSQL — already drop to a non-root user
# in their own entrypoints.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
AVD-DS-0002
